{
  "tema": 5989,
  "slug": "ser-para-proposito",
  "titulo": "Ser para for a purpose",
  "subtitulo": "¿Para qué es esto? Es para abrir latas.",
  "foto": "t04.jpg",
  "regla": "To say what something is for, use ser + para + an infinitive or a noun: es para cortar, es para la tabla. Never estar.",
  "comparada_kwiziq": null,
  "secciones": [
    {
      "id": "regla",
      "titulo": "The rule",
      "bloques": [
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "To say **what something is for** (its purpose), use **ser + para**."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "formula",
          "partes": [
            "thing",
            "+ ser + para +",
            "infinitive / noun"
          ]
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "English uses _-ing_ (_it's for cutting_); Spanish uses the **infinitive**: **es para cortar**."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "To ask, use **¿Para qué es?** = _What is it for?_ (also **¿Para qué sirve?**)."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "Never **estar**: **estar para** means something else (_to be about to_, _to be in the mood for_)."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "Tip: think of the label on a tool. The label always says **es para**..."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "ejemplos",
      "titulo": "Examples",
      "bloques": [
        {
          "tipo": "ejemplos",
          "lista": [
            {
              "es": "Este bloqueador ==es para== la cara.",
              "en": "This sunscreen is for your face."
            },
            {
              "es": "La cera ==es para== la tabla.",
              "en": "The wax is for the board."
            },
            {
              "es": "Estas tijeras ==son para== cortar tela.",
